Add CD Clock frequency control for VGA SOL initialization support

[Feature Description]
This change adds support for configuring higher CD Clock frequencies
(442MHz and 461MHz) for VGA SOL initialization during the Pre-Memory
phase. The feature allows BIOS to request specific display
core clock frequencies when VGA support is enabled during MRC training.

The VgaInitControl field in IGPU_PEI_PREMEM_CONFIG has been extended
to include BIT6-7 for CD Clock frequency selection:
- 0: No higher CD Clock required
- 1: 442 MHz
- 2: 461 MHz
- 3: Reserved

