MemoryTelemetry: Refactor PEIM to library and fix AMT PPR policy

[Issue Description]
The existing Memory Telemetry enabling AMT and PPR via a PEIM variable
was failing to set MRC AMT PPR to run. The PEIM variable MRC set was
overwritten during SA Policy update and AMT fails to run reliably.

[Resolution]
Refactored the architecture to eliminate the redundant PEIM and consolidate
all logic into PeiMemoryTelemetryLib. Created UpdateAmtPprMrcPolicy()
API that reads the AmtPprEnable UEFI variable and configures MRC policies:
- Sets MemConfigNoCrc->PprTestType.Value to PPR_TEST when AMT enabled
- Sets MemConfigNoCrc->PprRepairType to HARD_PPR or NOREPAIR_PPR based on
  AMT/PPR capability configuration

Modified PeiSaPolicyUpdatePreMem to call UpdateAmtPprMrcPolicy() when
PcdMemoryTelemetryEnabled is TRUE. If UpdateAmtPprMrcPolicy() succeeds,
the AMT-configured policies are preserved. If it fails (variable not found
or AMT not enabled), the code falls back to Setup menu values, maintaining
backward compatibility.

Package/Module:
MemoryTelemetryFeaturePkg, PlatSamplePkg, BoardPkg

[Impacted Platform]
ALL

